{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100, "noise": "L"}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 117, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Restoring the direct input-to-output residual path when it is missing yields far larger gains than swapping out an existing op on that edge."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "Deleting the input-output skip removes the cell's residual shortcut, which hurts much more than deleting a conv or pool on that edge."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Any op on edge 3 helps a lot when the direct path is absent, whereas replacing a skip with a conv loses the residual benefit."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a direct input-output path where none exists greatly improves gradient flow compared with replacing an existing edge-3 op."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Even a parameter-free path from input to output is valuable when the cell otherwise relies only on deep paths."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Without the direct input-output edge, removing edge 5 cuts one of the few remaining paths to the output and can collapse the cell."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "When edge 3 is absent the output depends on paths through node 1, so cutting edge 0 is much more destructive."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing a parameter-free pooling op with a learnable 3x3 conv adds much more capacity than replacing an existing conv or skip."}, {"edit_edge": 